# TODO / Ideas

## Move configuration out of the script (deferred, idea for later)

The configuration variables live in the header of `scan2file` (device,
AdditionalScanOptions, SaveFormat*, TempFormat, OllamaModel, Threshold,
BlankInkPercent). Anyone who adjusts them edits the script itself, so every
`git pull` collides with the local changes.

Idea: read values from `~/.config/scan2file.conf` (plain key=value, or INI
via configparser); the values in the script header stay as defaults.
Precedence: default < config file < command-line option.
The script can then be updated via git without losing one's own
configuration.

## Open

- OCR-only mode (`-m ocr`) is not implemented. `ocrscript` rebuilds the same
  chain in Bash. The obvious approach would be to read existing images/PDFs
  in as pages and use the rest of the scan2file pipeline unchanged.
- ADF (automatic document feeder) is not supported for multi-page scans.
  With the page model this comes almost for free: `scanimage
  --batch=<prefix>_%03d.pnm` scans the whole feeder, followed by
  `review_stack(pages, 0, args)` over all pages.

## Done (2026-09-13)

- PDFs came out as A3 instead of A4: PNM carries no DPI, magick assumed 72,
  and pdfsandwich clamped the 34x48-inch page to A3. Now `-density
  <resolution>` when merging, plus `-compress Group4` for B/W (roughly 50x
  smaller).
- Temp files were left behind when the output name contained `[` or `*`
  (glob metacharacters in the cleanup pattern). Now a dedicated directory
  via `tempfile.mkdtemp`, removed with `shutil.rmtree`.
- The scan resolution is passed to pdfsandwich as `-resolution` instead of
  it rasterizing internally at 300 dpi.
- `[v]` without an image viewer now reports that.
- Blank-page detection in color mode measures on a thresholded copy.
- Arrow and function keys are swallowed as a whole ESC sequence in
  `read_key` instead of being processed as three separate keys.
- Clean-ups: threshold as a parameter to `Page`, `pipe_to_chafa()` for both
  chafa calls, `-p/--progress/--no-progress` via BooleanOptionalAction,
  `ocr()` reports the exit code on failure, `output_file_exists` in
  snake_case.
